'' '#foreignlib' (fbc-modern RFC-0005) was reported as unimplemented and is not any
'' more. The grammar and the probe order are fbc's, read from fbForeignLibResolve:
''
''     #foreignlib ID (STATIC|DYNAMIC) "spec" (, "spec")*
''
'' A spec is a BASE NAME resolved against the directory of the source that wrote it,
'' then probed most-specific-first -- stem_<os>_<arch>, stem_<os>, stem_<arch>, stem
'' -- with the extensions the kind and target allow. "system:name" resolves nothing
'' and is handed to the linker as a bare name.
''
'' THE VARIANT ORDER IS WHAT THIS PINS. src/vendor holds probe_windows_x86_64.a,
'' probe_linux_x86_64.a AND probe_macos_arm64.a, so a build that ignored the os tag, or
'' took the plain stem, or picked by directory order, would resolve to the wrong file or
'' to none -- and the test runs for every target, so each has to choose its own.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO03

#foreignlib PROBE static "src/vendor/probe"
print "bound"
